Third-party material in this repository
=======================================

The Jet is (C) 1992 Dariusz Zolna / Tajemnice ATARI. The following files are
the original game or are derived from it and remain under the original
authors' copyright. They are included for preservation, study and
interoperability with the reconstruction; they are not licensed under the MIT
licence in LICENSE and no rights to them are granted by this repository:

  THEJET.LST            the hex listing as printed in Tajemnice ATARI 6-7/92,
                        from the disk image 6-7_92.atr in 6-7_92_listingi.zip
                        of the unofficial "Tajemnice Atari" electronic archive
                        (Pixel, 2001, https://tajemnice.atari8.info/6-7_92/)
  THEJET.COM            the binary the listing encodes (JET.OBJ of the
                        article), from the same disk image
  THEJET.PLA            the board printed with the article, from the same
                        disk image
  TheJet.bas            the listing as UTF-8 text taken from the HTML article
                        (identical to THEJET.LST line for line)
  plansze.txt           the board as text taken from the HTML article
                        (identical to THEJET.PLA)
  6-7_92_thejet.html    the magazine article containing the listing and the
                        board, as published by the archive
  thejet.obj, JET.COM   the binary decoded from the listing and the playable
                        file (binary + board), byte-identical to the archive's
  charset.bin, game.bin, text.bin, board.txt, meta.json, thejet/data/*
                        the segments of the binary, the board and the
                        parameters, as written by thejet_extract.py
  game.asm              disassembly of game.bin (the machine code is the
                        original author's; the labels and comments are ours)
  docs/*.png            screenshots rendered from the original graphics

The status line and the title screen of the original use the Atari 8-bit OS
character set, which is (C) Atari and is deliberately not part of this
repository; see --os-font in thejet/play.py.

If you are a rights holder and object to the inclusion of any of this material,
please open an issue and it will be removed.
